# Runtime authority

Temporal owns durable scheduling, retries, cancellation and replay. Domain and
application own admission, lifecycle, budgets, effects and settlement. Deep Agents
executes bounded operations through admitted bindings. Agent Server runs
subordinate graphs, never a second mission scheduler.

Application PostgreSQL owns control and immutable records. Temporal's database is
private runtime persistence. Redis is optional wake/fanout. Object storage carries
digest-bound payloads and directory bundles. External knowledge stays behind
admitted capability interfaces.

Local qualification uses the explicit transitional schema. Production common
startup stays blocked until the released common component and adapters qualify.
Runtime connections cannot migrate. See docs/knowledge/persistence.md.
